/-!
# QOU.Mass.BindingTauAnchorClosure — the wired selection-rule anchors force `τ > 2`

The depth-2 binding kernel `R(q,x) = x² − τx + 1` (det = 1,
`prop:sl2-prolongation-recurrence`) is generated by the **single** per-component
selection rule `a_D^(n) = lw(n−1)`, with the three production-wired anchors
(`binding_selection_rule_tau_closure.py`, witness
`binding-selection-rule-tau-closure.witness.json`):

* `a_D^(2) = lw(1) = 1`                         (muon / knot, c = 1);
* `a_D^(3) = lw(2) = (q+1)²/(3q)`               (Hopf-link, c = 2);
* `a_D^(4) = lw(3) = (3q² + 4 + 3q⁻²)/4`        (proton, Family-A — bit-for-bit the
  production VolDensity multiplier `linking_weight_family_a`, c = 3).

From the `det = 1` recurrence `a_D^(4) = τ·a_D^(3) − a_D^(2)` the trace is
`τ = (a_D^(2) + a_D^(4)) / a_D^(3)`. This file proves the two **algebraic** facts
that the Python script asserts numerically, now sorry-free over `ℝ`:

* `tauAnchor_closed_form` — `τ = 3(3q⁴ + 8q² + 3) / (4q(q+1)²)` (the corpus closed
  form; `≈ 2.6424` at `q₀`);
* `tauAnchor_gt_two` — `0 < q ⇒ 2 < τ`, holding throughout the substrate regime
  `q > 0` (not merely at `q₀`). The numerator obstruction is the
  sum-of-squares positivity `9q⁴ − 8q³ + 8q² − 8q + 9 > 0`
  (`504·(τ·den − 2·den) = 56(9q² − 4q)² + (56q − 36)² + 3240 > 0`).

Composing with `QOU.Mass.lambdaPlus_gt_one` (the abstract `τ > 2 ⇒ λ₊ > 1`
spectral bridge) discharges that bridge's hypothesis at the substrate: the binding
kernel is **extensive** (its dominant root `λ₊ > 1`) for every `q > 0`, given the
wired anchors — `binding_extensive_at_substrate`.

## Scope (honest — matches `binding_selection_rule_tau_closure.py`)

This formalises the **algebraic** half only: that the three wired anchor *values*
force this `τ` and that `τ > 2`. It does **not** derive the geometric residual —
that the prolonged Seiberg–Witten period `a_D^(n) = ∮ λ_SW^(n)` *equals* the
selection-rule value `lw(n−1)`, equivalently that this `τ` is the abelianised
`λ_SW` connection-holonomy trace on the coral elliptic curve `E_q`. That
identification is the open, owner-gated keystone object
(`conj:qdifference-kernel-prolongation-symbol`; the #1765 selection-rule
conjecture; cf. `docs/audits/2026-06-24-lever1-lambda-sw-no-shortcut.md`).

LaTeX label: `prop:binding-tau-anchor-closure`
(interprets `prop:binding-genfun-qdifference`).

## References
- [manuscript] §mass-theory/binding-genfun-qdifference
- [manuscript] §mass-theory/binding-selection-rule (witness
  `binding-selection-rule-tau-closure.witness.json`)
- [seiberg1994] https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(94)90124-4
-/

namespace QOU.Mass

open Real

/-- `a_D^(2) = lw(1) = 1` (muon / knot anchor, c = 1). -/
def aD2 : ℝ := 1

/-- `a_D^(3) = lw(2) = (q+1)²/(3q)` (Hopf-link anchor, c = 2). -/
noncomputable def aD3 (q : ℝ) : ℝ := (q + 1) ^ 2 / (3 * q)

/-- `a_D^(4) = lw(3) = (3q² + 4 + 3q⁻²)/4` (proton / Family-A anchor, c = 3). -/
noncomputable def aD4 (q : ℝ) : ℝ := (3 * q ^ 2 + 4 + 3 / q ^ 2) / 4

/-- The binding-kernel trace from the `det = 1` depth-2 recurrence
`a_D^(4) = τ·a_D^(3) − a_D^(2)`: `τ = (a_D^(2) + a_D^(4)) / a_D^(3)`. -/
noncomputable def tauAnchor (q : ℝ) : ℝ := (aD2 + aD4 q) / aD3 q

/-- **Closed form of the wired trace.** `τ = 3(3q⁴ + 8q² + 3) / (4q(q+1)²)`
(the corpus closed form; `≈ 2.6424` at `q₀`). -/
theorem tauAnchor_closed_form {q : ℝ} (hq : 0 < q) :
    tauAnchor q = 3 * (3 * q ^ 4 + 8 * q ^ 2 + 3) / (4 * q * (q + 1) ^ 2) := by
  have hq0 : q ≠ 0 := hq.ne'
  have hq1 : q + 1 ≠ 0 := by positivity
  unfold tauAnchor aD2 aD3 aD4
  field_simp
  ring

/-- **The wired trace exceeds `2` throughout the substrate regime.** For every
`q > 0`, `2 < τ`. The obstruction is the sum-of-squares positivity of the
numerator `9q⁴ − 8q³ + 8q² − 8q + 9`. -/
theorem tauAnchor_gt_two {q : ℝ} (hq : 0 < q) : 2 < tauAnchor q := by
  rw [tauAnchor_closed_form hq, lt_div_iff₀ (by positivity : (0 : ℝ) < 4 * q * (q + 1) ^ 2)]
  nlinarith [sq_nonneg (9 * q ^ 2 - 4 * q), sq_nonneg (56 * q - 36), hq, sq_nonneg q]

/-- **The binding kernel is extensive at the substrate.** Given the wired anchors,
the dominant root of `R(q,x) = x² − τx + 1` exceeds `1` for every `q > 0` — the
extensive (A-scaling) growth a saturating multiplicative trace (`τ = 2`, `λ = 1`)
cannot source. Composes `tauAnchor_gt_two` with the abstract spectral bridge
`lambdaPlus_gt_one`. -/
theorem binding_extensive_at_substrate {q : ℝ} (hq : 0 < q) :
    1 < lambdaPlus (tauAnchor q) :=
  lambdaPlus_gt_one (tauAnchor_gt_two hq)

end QOU.Mass
